Q: Argon2 hash verify using &#39;node:crypto&#39; module functions A: <p>This latest Argon2 implementation (since v24.7.0) seems to be a low-level implementation. At least, that's what can be figured out from the pull request <a href="https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/50353" rel="nofollow noreferrer">crypto: add argon2() and argon2Sync() methods</a>, check out <a href="https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/50353#issuecomment-1778260093" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this comment</a>. Maybe this will be expanded in later versions, so for now, you'll need to implement a hashing API with integrated PHC formatting and verify logic yourself.</p>
<p>An example of such an implementation is:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const { argon2Sync, randomBytes, timingSafeEqual } = require('node:crypto');

function hashPassword(password, { algorithm = 'argon2id', version = '19', parallelism = 4, memory = 65536, passes = 3, tagLength = 64, saltLength = 16, secret = Buffer.alloc(0) } = {}) {
    const nonce = randomBytes(saltLength);
    const params = { message: password, nonce: nonce, parallelism: parallelism, memory: memory, passes: passes, tagLength: tagLength, secret: secret };
    const hash = argon2Sync(algorithm, params);
    return [`$${algorithm}`, `v=${version}`, `m=${params.memory},t=${params.passes},p=${params.parallelism}`, toB64NoPad(nonce), toB64NoPad(hash)].join('$');
}

function verifyPassword(phcString, password, secret = Buffer.alloc(0)) {
    const phcParams = phcString.split('$');
    const argon2Params = Object.fromEntries(phcParams[3].split(',').map(p =&gt; p.split('=')));
    const nonce = Buffer.from(phcParams[4], 'base64');
    const hash = Buffer.from(phcParams[5], 'base64');
    const recalcHash = argon2Sync(phcParams[1], { message: password, nonce: nonce, memory: Number(argon2Params.m), passes: Number(argon2Params.t), parallelism: Number(argon2Params.p), tagLength: hash.length, secret: secret });
    return timingSafeEqual(hash, recalcHash);
}

function toB64NoPad(str) {
    return str.toString('base64').replace(/={1,2}$/, '');
}
</code></pre>
<p>which can be used as follows:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const secret = Buffer.from('some secret')
const password = 'my passphrase 1234'

let hash = hashPassword(password);
console.log('Hash:', hash);
console.log('Verified:', verifyPassword(hash, password));

hash = hashPassword(password, { algorithm: 'argon2i', saltLength: 8, tagLength: 32, memory: 131072, parallelism: 8, secret: secret});
console.log('Hash:', hash);
console.log('Verified:', verifyPassword(hash, password, secret));
</code></pre>
<p>Sample output:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Hash: $argon2id$v=19$m=65536,t=3,p=4$4Jwz02Jcpnkeur3aXrgy1g$TA0sJE8GfFjmQixhfTnKgFSgm7yoiwCEnrOirA/PLJ6JCLqqJT72OMey1FkTQ+7u5QqqgTPMJQwLwIEGZe+iTw
Verified: true
Hash: $argon2i$v=19$m=131072,t=3,p=8$SqcbVCmRZHI$Wf/LKnCjlxoY04en2/QgNgscHxKNyHHWS+abuE/C0wc
Verified: true
</code></pre>
<p>These hashes can also be successfully verified with the <a href="https://github.com/ranisalt/node-argon2" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Argon2 NPM module</a>:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const argon2NPM = require('argon2');

(async () =&gt; {
    const secret = Buffer.from('some secret')
    const password = 'my passphrase 1234'

    let hash = '$argon2id$v=19$m=65536,t=3,p=4$4Jwz02Jcpnkeur3aXrgy1g$TA0sJE8GfFjmQixhfTnKgFSgm7yoiwCEnrOirA/PLJ6JCLqqJT72OMey1FkTQ+7u5QqqgTPMJQwLwIEGZe+iTw'
    console.log('Verified:', await argon2NPM.verify(hash, password)); // true

    hash = '$argon2i$v=19$m=131072,t=3,p=8$SqcbVCmRZHI$Wf/LKnCjlxoY04en2/QgNgscHxKNyHHWS+abuE/C0wc'
    console.log('Verified:', await argon2NPM.verify(hash, password, { secret: secret })); // true
})();
</code></pre>
